BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-0-1795125600000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261119T220000Z
DTEND:20261119T221500Z
SUMMARY:Metro: Midosuji Line\, Namba → Shin-Osaka
DESCRIPTION:Osaka Metro Midosuji Line (M\, red) from Namba M20\, platform for 梅田・新大阪 (Umeda / Shin-Osaka)\, 7 stops to Shin-Osaka M13. Buy breakfast (ekiben) at Shin-Osaka before the 07:36.
LOCATION:Shin-Osaka Station
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Metro: Midosuji Line\, Namba → Shin-Osaka
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-1-1795127760000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261119T223600Z
DTEND:20261120T005700Z
SUMMARY:Shinkansen: Hikari 640\, 07:36 → Mishima 09:57\, reserved
DESCRIPTION:Tokaido Shinkansen Hikari 640 for 東京 Tokyo from Shin-Osaka\, 07:36\, to 三島 Mishima\, 09:57. The earliest direct train to Mishima (Hikari 636 does not stop there). Seat type: No designation (cabin-size bags fit the rack)
LOCATION:Mishima Station South Exit
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Shinkansen: Hikari 640\, 07:36 → Mishima 09:57\, reserved
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-2-1795137600000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T012000Z
DTEND:20261120T025000Z
SUMMARY:Bus: Mishima–Kawaguchiko Liner\, 10:20 → 11:50
DESCRIPTION:From the Shinkansen gates follow the signs to the South Exit (南口)\, 4 min. 特急 三島・河口湖ライナー (Mishima–Kawaguchiko Liner)\, stop 2 (2番線)\, 10:20 (23 min after the train: go straight there). It runs by Lake Yamanaka and Fuji-Q Highland to 河口湖駅 Kawaguchiko Station\, about 11:50\, the last stop\; it can run 10–20 min late in autumn traffic. Reserve the 6 seats ahead (¥2\,500 on the web\, ¥2\,700 otherwise)\; Suica is not accepted. One suitcase each in the trunk\, which cannot be reserved: queue first. If you miss it\, take the next one an hour later and skip Oishi Park. At Kawaguchiko\, put the suitcases in the coin lockers at the station (large lockers about ¥700\, est.): Fuga A only takes luggage from 13:00.
LOCATION:Kawaguchiko Station
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Bus: Mishima–Kawaguchiko Liner\, 10:20 → 11:50
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-3-1795144500000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T031500Z
DTEND:20261120T034200Z
SUMMARY:Bus: Red Line bus 12:15 → stop 20\, 12:42
DESCRIPTION:Red Line (河口湖周遊バス レッドライン) from the forecourt of Kawaguchiko Station at 12:15 (every 15 min: :00 :15 :30 :45\; 12:00 if the bus was on time\, 12:30 if it was late)\; tap Suica. It runs round the north shore past the Momiji Corridor (stop 17) to the last stop\, stop 20\, 河口湖自然生活館 (Oishi Park)\, 12:42. The Momiji festival makes these buses busy in mid-November: if one is full\, take the next. Sit on the left for the lake. Walk the lakeside flower path\, have the blueberry soft cream\, look from the café upstairs.
LOCATION:Oishi Park Kawaguchiko
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Bus: Red Line bus 12:15 → stop 20\, 12:42
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-4-1795150620000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T045700Z
DTEND:20261120T052400Z
SUMMARY:Bus: Red Line bus 13:57 Oishi Park → Kawaguchiko Station 14:24
DESCRIPTION:Red Line for 河口湖駅 from stop 20\, 河口湖自然生活館 at 13:57 (or 13:42 for a longer lunch)\, 27 min to Kawaguchiko Station. Suitcases\, two choices: (1) take them out of the lockers and walk them 2 min to Fuga A\, which takes luggage from 13:00 (check-in is from 16:00)\; or (2) leave them in the lockers and collect them when you come back at about 20:06\, which gives lunch 10–15 min more (lockers usually charge per day\, so about the same fee\; est.). Then houtou by the station and the 15:16 train. Be on a train by 15:16 at the latest\, or you reach the pagoda after sunset.
LOCATION:Kawaguchiko Station
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Bus: Red Line bus 13:57 Oishi Park → Kawaguchiko Station 14:24
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-5-1795155000000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T061000Z
DTEND:20261120T070000Z
SUMMARY:Train: Fujikyu Line 15:16 → Shimoyoshida ~15:30\, then walk and 398 steps
DESCRIPTION:Fujikyu Line (富士急行線) local from Kawaguchiko toward 大月 Otsuki at 15:16\, to 下吉田 Shimoyoshida\, about 15:30\; tap Suica. (Earlier: the 14:25 local\, or the 14:58 Fuji Kaiyu limited express\, which needs a limited-express ticket.) Follow the signs to 新倉山浅間公園 (Arakurayama Sengen Park)\, about 20 min on foot\, then 398 steps up to the deck above the pagoda. Go straight up: at 16:33 the sun sets to the right of Mt Fuji\, turning the pagoda and the mountain to silhouettes.
LOCATION:Chureito Pagoda Arakurayama Sengen Park
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Train: Fujikyu Line 15:16 → Shimoyoshida ~15:30\, then walk and 398 steps
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-6-1795160700000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T074500Z
DTEND:20261120T080000Z
SUMMARY:Walk: Walk down from the park to Honcho Street
DESCRIPTION:Leave the deck by about 16:45 and walk back down towards Shimoyoshida Station\, cross the tracks and continue to 本町通り (Honcho Street)\; the photo spot is the 本町二丁目 (Honcho 2-chome) crossing\, looking south along the street\, with Mt Fuji dark against the evening sky and the shop signs lit. Stay on the pavement. Walking time is an estimate.
LOCATION:Chureito Pagoda Arakurayama Sengen Park
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Walk: Walk down from the park to Honcho Street
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-7-1795163400000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T083000Z
DTEND:20261120T084500Z
SUMMARY:Walk: Walk to Nishiura (Shinsekai Kanpai-dori)
DESCRIPTION:Walk north from Honcho Street towards 月江寺 Gekkoji Station: the old Nishiura (西裏) nightlife quarter\, with the restored 新世界乾杯通り (Shinsekai Kanpai-dori) lane and small izakaya and yakitori bars on the streets around it. Nishiura is an area\, not one restaurant: walk the lanes and pick a place. Places are small: split into two groups of three\, or ask one place to seat six. Opening days are not checked: have a second choice.
LOCATION:Shinsekai Kanpai Dori Fujiyoshida
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Walk: Walk to Nishiura (Shinsekai Kanpai-dori)
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-8-1795171980000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T105300Z
DTEND:20261120T110600Z
SUMMARY:Train: Fujikyu Line 19:53 Shimoyoshida → Kawaguchiko ~20:06
DESCRIPTION:Fujikyu Line for 河口湖 Kawaguchiko from Gekkoji (about 19:55\, est.) or Shimoyoshida (19:53)\; trains also at 19:22\, 20:23\, 20:52\, 21:34\, the last at 23:51 from Shimoyoshida. Tap Suica. Check in at Fuga A (contactless\, 2 min on foot\; collect the suitcases from the station lockers first if you left them there)\, early night: the sunrise taxi is at 05:45.
LOCATION:Kawaguchiko Station
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Train: Fujikyu Line 19:53 Shimoyoshida → Kawaguchiko ~20:06
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-9-1795207500000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T204500Z
DTEND:20261120T210000Z
SUMMARY:Taxi: Pre-booked taxi from Fuga A
DESCRIPTION:No bus runs before 9:00. On Friday book a taxi for 05:45 at Fuga A: one 6-seat car if the company has one\, otherwise two taxis. Show the driver: 古賀政男記念公園 (富士河口湖町河口). About 10–15 min and roughly ¥2\,000–2\,500 per car (est.). Also book the pick-up at the Momiji Corridor for 07:35. Sunrise is about 06:25\; the summit turns pink a few minutes before.
LOCATION:Kogamasao Memorial Park Fujikawaguchiko
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Taxi: Pre-booked taxi from Fuga A
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-10-1795211280000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T214800Z
DTEND:20261120T220000Z
SUMMARY:Walk: Walk along the lake road to the Momiji Corridor
DESCRIPTION:Walk north-east along the lakeside road\, about 0.8 km (est.)\, to the Momiji Corridor (もみじ回廊) by the Kubota Itchiku Art Museum. The festival stalls open at 9:00\, so it is quiet\; the maples catch the early sun. Follow the map on your phone.
LOCATION:Momiji Corridor Kawaguchiko
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Walk: Walk along the lake road to the Momiji Corridor
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-11-1795214280000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T223800Z
DTEND:20261120T225000Z
SUMMARY:Taxi: Pre-booked taxi back to Fuga A
DESCRIPTION:Meet the taxi at 07:35 by the Momiji Corridor car park (or bus stop 17\, 久保田一竹美術館). About 10–15 min to Fuga A (est.). Breakfast\, pack\, check out by 08:25 and walk 2 min to bus stop 3 for the 08:40 bus.
LOCATION:Kawaguchiko Station
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Taxi: Pre-booked taxi back to Fuga A
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-12-1795218000000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261120T234000Z
DTEND:20261121T012500Z
SUMMARY:Bus: Highway bus\, Kawaguchiko Station 08:40 → Busta Shinjuku 10:25
DESCRIPTION:Shinjuku–Fuji Five Lakes highway bus (新宿–富士五湖線) for バスタ新宿. Board at stop 3 (3のりば) in the forecourt of Kawaguchiko Station\, 08:40\; be at the stop by 08:30 and show the booking on your phone. It stops at Fuji-Q Highland (08:48)\, then runs up the Chuo Expressway. Arrive Busta Shinjuku 10:25\, at the 3rd-floor arrival deck (新宿駅南口・3階おりば). Direct\, no changes\, suitcases go in the hold. All seats reserved: book 6 seats ahead. The next bus is 09:10 → 10:55
LOCATION:Shinjuku Southern Terrace
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Bus: Highway bus\, Kawaguchiko Station 08:40 → Busta Shinjuku 10:25
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-13-1795224900000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261121T013500Z
DTEND:20261121T020000Z
SUMMARY:Train: Sagawa counter\, then JR Yamanote Line to Harajuku
DESCRIPTION:On the 3rd floor of Busta Shinjuku\, where the bus arrives\, go into the Tokyo Tourist Information Center: the Sagawa counter (6:30–21:00) sends suitcases to a Tokyo hotel the same day if you hand them in by 11:00\; they reach Grids Tokyo Ueno after 16:00 (about ¥2\,180 for a suitcase up to 140 cm and 20 kg\; counted in the budget). If you would rather not send them\, or the bus is late and you miss 11:00\, leave them in storage at the same counter (about ¥800–1\,500 a bag for the day) or in coin lockers\, and collect them on the way back through Shinjuku before 21:00 (then JR to Ueno with the suitcases). Then go down to the JR gates below the terminal: JR Yamanote Line\, platform 14\, toward 渋谷・品川 (Shibuya / Shinagawa)\, 2 stops to Harajuku JY19\, ~4 min.
LOCATION:Meiji Jingu
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Train: Sagawa counter\, then JR Yamanote Line to Harajuku
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jp-trip-14-1795232400000@trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T080400Z
DTSTART:20261121T034000Z
DTEND:20261121T040000Z
SUMMARY:Walk: Walk via Omotesando
DESCRIPTION:Walk down Omotesando towards Aoyama\, turn left on Aoyama-dori to the Aoyama 2-chome corner: the ginkgo avenue runs north from there.
LOCATION:Icho Namiki Jingu Gaien
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Walk: Walk via Omotesando
TRIGGER:-PT15M
